      "math_academy_id": "q-134164",
      "knowledge_point_id": "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Speed of an Object",
      "problem": "A canoe traveled $280$ feet in $70$ seconds at a constant rate.  What is the speed of the canoe?",
      "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in feet per second), we divide the number of feet, $280,$ by the number of seconds, $70.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{280}{70}=280÷70=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the canoe is $4$ feet per second.",
