      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time",
      "problem": "It takes $30$ minutes for a slug to crawl $135$ centimeters when moving at a constant pace. Find the distance this slug covers in $18$ minutes.",
      "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in centimeters per minute, we divide the number of centimeters, $135,$ by the number of minutes, $30.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{135}{30} & =135÷30 \\\\  & =\\frac{135÷15}{30÷15} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =9÷2 \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the slug is $4.5$ centimeters per minute. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $18$ minutes, we multiply the speed by $18.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =4.5\\times 18 \\\\  & =81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slug covers $81$ centimeters in $18$ minutes.",
